{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017B88tkLMKKyCkmuJxwxr2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Crucible Stage 1 â€” Master Plan: Aurora Awareness Revamp\n\n**Plan shape**\n- A 5-wave plan, each wave independently shippable, ordered by value-per-effort Ã— North-Star urgency: W1 model surface â†’ W2 collection fix â†’ W3 benchmarks â†’ W4 awareness+value â†’ W5 minimal adoption.\n- A sixth wave (W6, the \"map\") was locked **IN-but-optional** at Stage 0; the Shark Tank recommended **deferring it** out of this run.\n- Stage 1 approval gate posed four decisions to John: approve the resequenced 5 waves; defer-vs-keep W6; accept the adoption shrink (labels + decision-logging now, Helping-Hand auto-adoption later); and any reweighting of wave order.\n\n**North-Star inclusion mapping** (from the anchor table)\n- W1 serves NS1+NS2; W2 serves NS1+NS4; W3 serves NS1+NS2+NS3(fit); W4 serves NS1+NS5; W5 serves NS3 (with labels feeding NS4). W6 was rated only a weak NS1 contributor â€” consistent with the defer recommendation.\n\n**Wave 3 â€” Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view** *(NS2)* â€” shipped GREEN 2026-06-12\n- Intent: turn the model price-sheet into a decision tool by joining a license-clean benchmark slice â†’ \"best-for-X\" cards (best coding / agentic / cheap-good / long-context / open-weights), each justified.\n- Sources: OpenRouter `/models` (specs/pricing, **transient-enrich only, never redistributed** per CC1) + Epoch AI CC-BY benchmarks (GPQA Diamond, SWE-bench Verified, FrontierMath, MATH-L5, AIME).\n- **Schema BLOCKER (Stage-2 verified):** live `model_benchmarks` had `source_url`/`scored_at`/`observed_at`/`contamination_flag` but **no `source` and no `license`** column, and `benchmark_scraper.py` inserted without them. Fixed by migration `0027_benchmark_provenance.sql` (idempotent; schema.sql mirrored), with a single insert chokepoint `roles/benchmark_ingest.py::insert_benchmark` enforcing CC5 provenance.\n- Composite is **sparse-aware**: computed only where component coverage exists, with coverage/missing shown explicitly â€” no single black-box index, no false authority over missing cells.\n- CC1 no-leak rule (Epoch CC-BY redistributable; Artificial-Analysis- and OpenRouter-derived data NOT) was **verified in both directions through the real publisher** â€” load-bearing.\n- Execution path: EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator gate â†’ 2 reviewers (E GO on CC1/CC5 provenance; F NO-GO with 1 BLOCKER + 1 MAJOR and a failing repro) â†’ FIX â†’ re-gate â†’ orchestrator re-verify. **Gate moved 1108 â†’ 1120 passed** (+12 additive; one pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure left untouched).\n\n**Wave 5 â€” Minimal, honest adoption (decisions + labels)** *(NS3, deliberately small)* â€” shipped GREEN 2026-06-12\n- Decision content lives **in the report**: top-candidate card fields (what-it-is / fit / recommendation+confidence / advantages / risks / provenance / effort). Recommendation is an explicitly **non-authoritative suggestion, never a consensus verdict**.\n- **Delivered** migration `0028_decisions.sql` â€” `decisions(id, artifact_id FK, decision_type CHECK IN ('adopt','defer','reject','retire'), reason, explicit_label, explicit_confidence, made_at, made_by_session_id, recorded_at)`. The table doubles as the label source feeding Wave 2's deferred weight-validation.\n- **No Helping-Hand auto-adoption** in this run â€” that's a **future gate at nâ‰¥30** accepted decisions; current n=7 deliberately forbids automation.\n- Execution path: EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator gate â†’ 2 reviewers (I = CC1/Â§B-2/anti-test-weakening; J = capture correctness + production-safety; **both GO**) â†’ 1 bounded hardening FIX â†’ re-gate. **Gate moved 1135 â†’ 1152 passed** (+17 additive; same single pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure).\n\n**Cross-cutting**\n- Both shipped waves followed the same Crucible/Foreman discipline: orchestrator-run test gate (never a sub-agent), â‰¥2 heterogeneous reviewers with â‰¥2-agree on blockers, additive-only gate movement, and an untouched pre-existing `runs` failure carried forward as a known unrelated baseline.\n\n---\nA note on grounding: this summary is built from the anchors you supplied. The three member documents (Execution Log, Master Plan, Implementation Plan) weren't included in full, so I summarized the anchored excerpts rather than the documents end-to-end. If you want me to read the actual files (e.g. under `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/`) and reconcile the summary against them, point me at the paths."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4260,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9452,"cache_read_input_tokens":20861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9452},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a5ce3d5-0c68-401e-8019-d7034476f16d","uuid":"089bf26f-82ba-48ea-afa5-117ee8dd3d3b","request_id":"req_011Cc9Wbc4iC7WnqYLFt9bRP"}
